#VIC20 Local Console Commands
#(C) 2022 Ignacio Cea Fornies
?./Standard.hlp
?./Commodore.hlp
;VIA1
To know the status of the VIA1 chip.
Parameters: None.
;VIA2
To know the status of the VIA2 chip.
Parameters: None.
;SCREENDUMP
To know the content of the screen.
Parameters: None.
;COLORDUMP
To know the content of the color screen.
Parameters: None.
;CHARSDRAW [c1 c2 c3 ...]
To print out the characters data.
Parameters:
=> None: Draw all characters.
=> [c1 c2 c3 ...] (optional): Draw just the characters listed. From 0 to 255.
;LIGHTPEN ON|OFF
To active/desactivate the connection of a lightpen.
Lightpen can work at the same time that joysticks (something that doesn't happen in real C64!),
because it is emulated using the MOUSE (where left button means "pressing the lightpen against the screen").
Lightpen is disconnected by default.
Parameters:
=> ON|OFF (mandatory): Whether to activate or to desactivate the lightpen.